# Spot-Lyric lyrics server configuration. Copy to server/.env (keep it private).

# ---- Storage: Cloudflare R2 (or any S3-compatible bucket) ------------------
# Every shared match ("使用此歌词" or the upload button in the client) is one
# object: lyrics/<spotify-track-id>.json holding the Spotify link, the chosen
# NetEase / QQ song and its lyrics. Matching itself runs in the client.
# Create the bucket:  cf r2 buckets create --name spot-lyric
# Credentials: an API token with "Workers R2 Storage Bucket Item Read + Write"
# on the bucket. Access key ID = token ID, secret = SHA-256 hex of the token value.
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
R2_BUCKET=spot-lyric
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# Other S3-compatible storage (MinIO, ...): set the endpoint instead of the account id.
# R2_ENDPOINT=https://<account-id>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
# R2_PREFIX=lyrics/
# Without any bucket the server stores matches in /data/objects (docker volume).

# ---- Access ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional shared secret. When set, clients must enter it in
# 歌词设置 > 歌词服务器 > 令牌.
# API_TOKEN=
# Browser origins allowed to call the API (the Spotify desktop client).
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://xpui.app.spotify.com
# Requests per minute per client address (all endpoints / bind + unbind / relay).
# RATE_LIMIT=240
# WRITE_RATE_LIMIT=30
# RELAY_RATE_LIMIT=120
# Trust CF-Connecting-IP / X-Forwarded-For (behind Cloudflare Tunnel or a proxy).
# TRUST_PROXY=1

# ---- Relay -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Spotify's renderer may not call NetEase / QQ itself (CORS). Clients then send
# the request they built to POST /api/relay and the server forwards it verbatim
# (allow-listed hosts and API paths only). 0 disables the relay: such clients
# then need Spotify started with --disable-web-security (patch.sh --direct).
# RELAY=1
# NetEase returns encrypted search results to non-mainland addresses unless a
# mainland X-Real-IP is sent. Empty disables the header.
# NETEASE_REAL_IP=211.161.244.70
# Minimum spacing between requests to each provider (QQ throttles bursts per IP).
# QQ_MIN_INTERVAL_MS=400
# NETEASE_MIN_INTERVAL_MS=120
# In-memory cache of stored objects (MB). Nothing is cached on disk.
# CACHE_MB=64

# ---- docker compose --------------------------------------------------------
# Host address / port the container is published on.
# BIND_ADDRESS=127.0.0.1
# HOST_PORT=38917
# Cloudflare Tunnel token for the optional "tunnel" profile.
# TUNNEL_TOKEN=
